# d810-cobra published release identity -- THE single source of truth.
#
# Everything that names a published d810-cobra artifact derives from this file:
# the image bake (docker/cobra-bake/cobra_identity.sh, and through it the image
# build script and the Dockerfile build args/labels), the Docker test runner's
# accepted-wheel table, and the tests of both. Nothing re-declares these values.
#
# Format: whitespace-separated columns, '#' comments, blank lines ignored. That
# is deliberate. It is the only shape both bash (a `while read -r` loop -- no
# jq, no dependency, and no shell-sourcing of a data file) and Python
# (str.split) parse without a second copy or a parser. JSON would force jq,
# which is not guaranteed on the host, or an eval-based shell hack; a
# `sha256sum -c` file cannot carry the commits.
#
# The preflight wheels built before the 0.1.5 release carry the SAME filenames
# and the SAME sizes as the published ones and differ only in their bytes, so
# only the sha256 separates them. They are provenance evidence and must never
# appear here:
#   b71d40e45146004a968a96a1b17493b16ac04f2a98e41c12a1f87a38ddf3ab25  aarch64
#   c642e6a6d61f8b841d97df78375c6e1da43fc05a56c3b68218230ed23beaa762  x86_64
#
# tag_commit is the build/tag commit of the published release (tag v0.1.5).
# core_commit is the CoBRA core (third_party/cobra) commit it was built over.
# parent_commit is the d810-cobra source revision the runner pins for source
# builds; a baked image must name it, or a baked run and a source-built run are
# not comparable measurements.
#
# columns: arch sha256 version tag_commit core_commit parent_commit wheel_filename
